{
  "text": " My name is Jeff Childers. I'm a commercial litigation attorney practicing in a small practice in Gainesville, Florida. I was the farthest from qualified to work on any of these freedom related or health and autonomy related issues three years ago. I got dragged into it here when my local county implemented some mandates that I disagreed with and I found my very first complaint against a government entity that I'd ever done. The result of that is we won several cases and we were able to make things better for a whole lot of people in this area and you know one of the things that really motivates me to continue in this direction is that this kind of work has been some of the most personally and professionally rewarding work that I've ever done. I'd like to encourage you to come attend the conference because what we're trying to do here is help people get up to speed faster. I'm going to share my experience and kind of what it took for me to get up to speed and I'm also going to share about how I've been rewarded in so many ways and all the different benefits that I've experienced as a lawyer in practicing in these areas and how it has really enhanced my practice rather than taking anything away from it. So I think all of us are apprehensive about entering a new practice area and rightfully so but this is an area that is critically important at this time in our lives. It's an opportunity that will probably never be presented with again and I invite you to come and take a listen and see if it sounds like something that might work for you.",
